Phase 6.2 adapts the following Mika concepts, re-written in Kotlin for ONYX (no files copied verbatim):
  - RefStabilizer (stable element refs across screen re-reads)
      -> core/screen/.../ScreenReliability.kt (StableRefs), ScreenSession.resolveRef
  - OperationGuards / Fingerprints (no-effect, revisit and cycle guards; screen fingerprints)
      -> core/screen/.../ScreenReliability.kt (TaskGuards), core/runtime/.../phone/MacroMatch.kt (ScreenFingerprint)
  - ScreenDiagnosis (screens that need a human: password, verification code, payment, captcha, protected)
      -> core/screen/.../ScreenReliability.kt (HandoffDetector)
  - ActionEffect / UntilWait / BatchRunner (code-checked waits and action effects, step batches)
      -> core/runtime/.../phone/MacroReplay.kt (MacroPlayer), ScreenSession action "effect"

