0.6.2.3 adapts the following MAFDET ideas, re-written in Kotlin/C++ for ONYX (no code or text copied):
  - Reading ahead: the KV cache follows the draft while the user types (longest common token prefix kept, only the
    changed tail computed), so Send only evaluates what is left
      -> core/inference/.../TypeAhead.kt (PrefixMath, TypeAheadController), EngineInferenceAdapter.prefill,
         engine/llamacpp/src/main/cpp/llama_jni.cpp (nativePrefill; aborted prefill keeps its finished batches)
  - Reasoning ahead: a think-block frame that asks for material per key term / name / number, a "New words" line per
    change, a "message is complete" sentence on Enter, a small negative logit bias on meta words, and closing the
    think block the way the chat template does when the model ends its turn inside it
      -> core/inference/.../TypeAhead.kt (ReasoningAhead, ReasoningAheadSession), EngineInferenceAdapter.reasonAhead

Third-party native code (llama.cpp, KleidiAI) keeps its own license files under third_party/.
